    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d890">

                <pb facs="1689" n="1649" xml:id="pg1649"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">684A.85/9–454: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 890<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the
                        Embassy in Israel</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d890-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-09-04T14:37:00-04:00">September 4, 1954—2:37
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>143. Acting Asst Secy NEA advised Israel Chargé fourth as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p><hi rendition="#italic">Begin summary:</hi> Dept views with great concern
                            reports organized and armed force Israel military numbering several
                            hundred conducted operations Jordan territory area villages Beit Sira,
                            Beit Liqya and Khirbet al Misbah early morning Sept 2.</p>
                        <p>It is realized infiltrators from Jordan continue constitute serious
                            problem Israel, particularly to inhabitants agricultural settlements
                            close to HKJ-Israel armistice line. At same time it must be said
                            Israel’s apparent policy of organized and armed retaliation has not only
                            already been condemned but it has also brought about heightened rather
                            than reduced tensions along armistice line.</p>
                        <p>It is to interest US as well as peoples of area that there be reduction
                            these tensions and, step-by-step move toward peace between Israel and
                            her neighbors. Peace in NE must be painstakingly built through measures
                            calculated diminish areas conflict and lessen hatreds. Armed retaliatory
                            raids not such measures.</p>
                        <p>Dept strongly hopes Israel will abandon armed retaliation, and that both
                            Israel and Jordan will cooperate wholeheartedly with appropriate UN
                            organs in enforcement of General Armistice Agreement. <hi
                                rendition="#italic">End summary</hi>.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Dept does not intend release foregoing to press but question from press at Sept 7
                    conference re reason for Shiloah’s call will be answered if it arises along
                    above lines. Tel Aviv may in its discretion make similar statement to IG. Amman
                    and other addressees Arab states authorized informally advise Govts of action
                    taken, if deemed useful.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d890-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d890-f1-content">
                <p>Sent also to Amman priority, Beirut, Baghdad, Cairo, Damascus, Jidda, London, and
                    Paris.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
